<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  gba_bench: the standalone harness of the integrated GBA emulator (issue #388).

  It builds the GBA core (src/gba, without the SDL front end) together with the test runner and the
  ROM harness in testing/gba_bench, exactly like testing/gba_bench/build.sh does on Linux.

  The core sources are compiled here rather than linked from the GBA library project on purpose:
  the library also holds gba_sdl.cpp, which would drag SDL2 into a harness that is meant to be a
  plain console application with no third party dependency at all.

  Run it from the scripts/VS2026 directory (or from Visual Studio's Test/Debug). Its command line
  options - the unit tests, the boot ROM animation, a PNG dump, a benchmark - are the same as the
  ones testing/gba_bench/check.sh passes to the Linux build; see testing/gba_bench/Readme.md.
-->
